    "narrative": "LawDog enters June 11th with a tight, utility-heavy lineup as we navigate a slate defined by moderate matchups. The primary engine for today is **Geraldo Perdomo**, who leads our active starters with a score of 55.17. While he lacks the power upside of some teammates, his position in the heart of the order and a favorable matchup against Phillips (xERA 4.33) provide the highest floor of the day. **Taylor Ward** offers the most significant ceiling at 52.92 despite a tricky date with Woo (xERA 3.42). While the matchup against the Seattle right-hander is suboptimal, the park factor provides a substantial +16% boost to his base projection, though the 42% rain risk necessitates a close watch of pre-game alerts.\n\nOn the middle infield, **Masyn Winn** (49.02) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.56) remain locked in as volume plays. **Masyn Winn**\u2019s efficiency is buoyed by a manageable matchup against Scott, and he remains a priority given our league\u2019s obsession with stolen base production. Conversely, **Gleyber Torres** faces the stiffest headwind today; the negative dynamic platoon shift (-13%) against Matthews effectively nullifies his benefit from batting second in the order. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler** all sidelined due to team off-days or injury designations, our bench depth is currently non-existent, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. If **Taylor Ward**'s rain risk materializes, we lack the immediate bench reinforcement to pivot, making today a high-stakes deployment of our core assets.",
